From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:51:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: samsung: zuma: ALIVE has no GPIO interrupts

All of zuma's ALIVE banks are wake-up EINT banks, each pin on its own
GIC interrupt, so the controller has no interrupt for GPIO EINTs.
exynos_eint_gpio_init() only serves EINT_TYPE_GPIO banks, and without
an interrupt on the controller node it logs "irq number not available"
at every boot. Drop it from ALIVE, as gs101's ALIVE controller does.

Fixes: 6d5bc3a01525 ("pinctrl: samsung: Add Tensor G3 pin banks")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/samsung/pinctrl-exynos-arm64.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/samsung/pinctrl-exynos-arm64.c b/drivers/pinctrl/samsung/pinctrl-exynos-arm64.c
index 74bcc3806..bab951eb0 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/samsung/pinctrl-exynos-arm64.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/samsung/pinctrl-exynos-arm64.c
@@ -2658,7 +2658,6 @@ static const struct samsung_pin_ctrl zuma_pin_ctrl[] __initconst = {
 		/* Controller 0: ALIVE */
 		.pin_banks	= zuma_pin_alive,
 		.nr_banks	= ARRAY_SIZE(zuma_pin_alive),
-		.eint_gpio_init	= exynos_eint_gpio_init,
 		.eint_wkup_init	= exynos_eint_wkup_init,
 	}, {
 		/* Controller 1: CUSTOM */
